 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Test 3, Question 2 · Discrete conditional distributions and conditional expectation** (10 marks)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "8cc29a63-4a99-5dd1-a9a1-bd19630be1c7"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "\"Given $Y=y$\" means: you already know $Y$. Keep only the outcomes with that $y$, and rescale them so they add to $1$. That new PMF gives probabilities, a CDF, and an average.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4b9b07db-4d41-52b5-8f87-967e9f76f17d"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "tone": "tip",
   "text": "**Formula sheet lines for this question:**\n\n$$\np_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{p_{X,Y}(x,y)}{p_Y(y)}\n$$\n\n$$\nF_X(x)=\\sum_{t\\le x}p_X(t)\\qquad\\text{(use it with }p_{X|Y}\\text{ for the conditional CDF)}\n$$\n\n$$\nE[X\\mid Y=y]=\\sum_x x\\,p_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)\n$$\n\nExpect: **conditional PMF → conditional CDF or probability → $E[X\\mid Y=y]$ → independent?**",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "2697ea6d-6161-5930-a05b-3319b9b5f11f"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part A · Conditional PMF",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9aa15e09-c37b-581f-9058-4480493d57da"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "A1 · From a table",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "955bee7b-18cb-559d-b705-36a61b9dcae8"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{p_{X,Y}(x,y)}{p_Y(y)}",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "37d793a5-49d8-46c7-8cd4-a136e4202f08"
    }
   ],
   "id": "cdffe2e6-1fa3-567e-9d62-c2f2392958c5"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Select** the row or column of the given value.",
    "**Total** it. That total is $p_Y(y)$.",
    "**Divide** each cell in it by the total. The new numbers add to $1$."
   ],
   "ordered": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "0fb9e19e-b549-550b-804e-d1d2eab4e12e"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 1 · Given a column, given a row ★ (Lecture 17 / Tutorial 7 table)",
   "prompt": "Find $p_{X|Y}(x\\mid1)$ and $p_{Y|X}(y\\mid1)$.\n\n| | $y=0$ | $y=1$ | $y=2$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $x=0$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $x=1$ | $0.20$ | $0.30$ | $0.20$ |",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Given $Y=1$:** column $y=1$ is $0.15,\\ 0.30$. Total $0.45$.",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(0\\mid1)=\\frac{0.15}{0.45}=\\frac13,\\qquad p_{X|Y}(1\\mid1)=\\frac{0.30}{0.45}=\\frac23"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Given $X=1$:** row $x=1$ is $0.20,\\ 0.30,\\ 0.20$. Total $0.70$.",
     "latex": "p_{Y|X}(y\\mid1)=\\frac27,\\ \\frac37,\\ \\frac27\\quad(y=0,1,2)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac13,\\ \\tfrac23$; $\\tfrac27,\\ \\tfrac37,\\ \\tfrac27$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "a25bde00-9c60-4121-8f33-54a29f5be927"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c9adc2c3-19a1-5e7b-8097-a0eb9e80d169"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 1 · Your turn",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "Same table. Find $p_{X|Y}(x\\mid2)$ and $p_{Y|X}(y\\mid0)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Column $y=2$:** $0.05,\\ 0.20$, total $0.25$.",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid2)=0.2,\\ 0.8\\quad(x=0,1)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Row $x=0$:** $0.10,\\ 0.15,\\ 0.05$, total $0.30$.",
     "latex": "p_{Y|X}(y\\mid0)=\\frac13,\\ \\frac12,\\ \\frac16\\quad(y=0,1,2)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$0.2,\\,0.8$; $\\tfrac13,\\,\\tfrac12,\\,\\tfrac16$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "bc5cca26-60bf-5245-b866-72937b0a4b86"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "A2 · From an experiment",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "43a1c7fd-f5c1-5f0d-83c1-d45de7f21eb6"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "No table? List the equally likely outcomes that fit the condition, then count.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "d8eb7f26-b3eb-4d3d-8c18-85f2099a37cb"
    }
   ],
   "id": "41fdec95-6adf-5914-a725-c4ff273a0ab4"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{\\#\\text{ outcomes with }X=x\\text{ and }Y=y}{\\#\\text{ outcomes with }Y=y}",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e06cd12d-c198-566a-9ee2-331579220b0b"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 2 · Two dice ★ (Lecture 21)",
   "prompt": "Roll two fair dice. $X$ = first die, $Y$ = sum. Find $p_{X|Y}(x\\mid7)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Outcomes with sum $7$:** $(1,6),(2,5),(3,4),(4,3),(5,2),(6,1)$. That is $6$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Each $x$ appears once.**",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid7)=\\frac16,\\qquad x=1,2,\\ldots,6\\quad(0\\text{ otherwise})"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac16$ for $x=1,\\ldots,6$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "d8eb7f26-b3eb-4d3d-8c18-85f2099a37cb"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1d5acd9d-c768-4d3b-a08d-e5ff6d4b40ce"
    }
   ],
   "id": "ef796f20-e880-52e2-aa1f-576092d5fd94"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 2 · Three coins",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "Toss a fair coin 3 times. $X$ = number of heads, $Y=1$ if the first toss is heads, else $0$. Find $p_{X|Y}(x\\mid1)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Outcomes with first toss $H$:** $HHH,\\ HHT,\\ HTH,\\ HTT$ (4 of them).",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Count heads:** $3,\\ 2,\\ 2,\\ 1$.",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid1)=\\frac14,\\ \\frac24,\\ \\frac14\\quad(x=1,2,3)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac14,\\ \\tfrac12,\\ \\tfrac14$ at $x=1,2,3$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "13802d67-6710-598b-83ea-968396693df4"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "A3 · Independence from the conditional PMF",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "5e6b6302-72ff-56f0-9123-96266631ee1d"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Independent means knowing $Y$ changes nothing:",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "37d793a5-49d8-46c7-8cd4-a136e4202f08"
    }
   ],
   "id": "e84ad74b-585f-5bac-ba3a-725b4d0d1fb1"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=p_X(x)\\quad\\text{for every }x\\text{ and every possible }y",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9931be1a-330f-533c-bd6c-910aa6617cbf"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "One mismatch → dependent.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "32859ed2-1dbd-52e7-9333-0b2a0d921af2"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 3 · The dice are dependent ★ (Lecture 21)",
   "prompt": "$X$ = first die, $Y$ = sum. Are $X$ and $Y$ independent?",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Pick an extreme $y$.** $Y=2$ forces $(1,1)$.",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(1\\mid2)=1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Compare** with no information.",
     "latex": "p_X(1)=\\frac16\\ne1"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Not independent",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1d5acd9d-c768-4d3b-a08d-e5ff6d4b40ce"
    }
   ],
   "id": "86e1e2e4-875c-549d-ad4e-b680ada70dc1"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 3 · Table check",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "In the A1 table, compare $p_{X|Y}(0\\mid1)$ with $p_X(0)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "From A1, $p_{X|Y}(0\\mid1)=\\tfrac13$. The row total is $p_X(0)=0.30$.",
     "latex": "\\frac13\\ne0.30\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\\text{dependent}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Dependent",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "228bfe0b-6ada-562e-a999-b2d905f1e6a3"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part B · Conditional CDF",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "1bb2efca-5651-54b7-a5b5-148b6a4b7a31"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Add the conditional PMF up to and including $x$. It is a staircase.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "37d793a5-49d8-46c7-8cd4-a136e4202f08"
    }
   ],
   "id": "fd77495e-92e6-5a5a-8ac7-a3dcc86d7656"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "F_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=P(X\\le x\\mid Y=y)=\\sum_{t\\le x}p_{X|Y}(t\\mid y)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "c8c02aea-f063-57cf-85a2-1505595ea68a"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "Jump at each possible value, flat in between. $0$ before the first value, $1$ after the last.",
    "Use $\\le$ at each step: write \"$1\\le x<2$\", not \"$1<x\\le2$\".",
    "Discrete only: $P(X<2\\mid\\cdot)$ is **not** $F(2\\mid\\cdot)$. It is $F(1\\mid\\cdot)$ when the values are integers."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "0df4c51e-2541-534a-866b-818950efa569"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 4 · Dice ★ (Lecture 21)",
   "prompt": "$X$ = first die, $Y$ = sum. Find $F_{X|Y}(x\\mid7)$ and $P(X\\le3\\mid Y=7)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**From A2:** $\\tfrac16$ at each of $1,\\ldots,6$. **Add up.**",
     "latex": "F_{X|Y}(x\\mid7)=\\begin{cases}0,&x<1\\\\ \\frac16,&1\\le x<2\\\\ \\frac26,&2\\le x<3\\\\ \\frac36,&3\\le x<4\\\\ \\frac46,&4\\le x<5\\\\ \\frac56,&5\\le x<6\\\\ 1,&x\\ge6\\end{cases}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Read off.**",
     "latex": "P(X\\le3\\mid Y=7)=F_{X|Y}(3\\mid7)=\\frac36=\\frac12"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Staircase in steps of $\\tfrac16$; $\\tfrac12$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "1d5acd9d-c768-4d3b-a08d-e5ff6d4b40ce"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c10f9a0d-a9b4-57b5-819f-127b4987a19f"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 4 · CDF from a table",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "Use $p_{Y|X}(y\\mid1)=\\tfrac27,\\tfrac37,\\tfrac27$ at $y=0,1,2$ (A1). Find $F_{Y|X}(y\\mid1)$ and $P(Y<2\\mid X=1)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Add up.**",
     "latex": "F_{Y|X}(y\\mid1)=\\begin{cases}0,&y<0\\\\ \\frac27,&0\\le y<1\\\\ \\frac57,&1\\le y<2\\\\ 1,&y\\ge2\\end{cases}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**$Y<2$** means $Y\\le1$.",
     "latex": "P(Y<2\\mid X=1)=F_{Y|X}(1\\mid1)=\\frac57"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Staircase $\\tfrac27,\\tfrac57,1$; $\\tfrac57$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "62bbe952-b310-59c9-990c-f3dcec55fae4"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part C · Conditional expectation",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "6d9b475c-7075-510d-89db-e4616a103345"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "C1 · $E[X\\mid Y=y]$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b33e748c-7289-5388-869e-46d0de9e8743"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "The average of $X$ using the **conditional** probabilities as weights.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "5ad2282c-1474-44fa-ad34-94fab76cd986"
    }
   ],
   "id": "af13e928-bf28-5c8f-95bf-dc53d4761a4a"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\sum_x x\\,p_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "a9f5c14a-5577-5e2b-a1f0-4cda4c2c3ebc"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "For one value ($Y=7$) it is a number. With $y$ left as a letter it can be a formula in $y$.",
    "Independent → $E[X\\mid Y=y]=E[X]$ for every $y$. So if it changes with $y$, they are **dependent**."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "5d2653d8-7de1-5669-a89f-3c0a41d42ede"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 5 · Dice and a table ★ (Lecture 22)",
   "prompt": "**(a)** $X$ = first die, $Y$ = sum. Find $E[X\\mid Y=7]$.\n\n**(b)** In the A1 table, find $E[Y\\mid X=1]$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Weights** $\\tfrac16$ each (A2).",
     "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=7]=\\frac{1+2+3+4+5+6}{6}=3.5"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Weights** $\\tfrac27,\\tfrac37,\\tfrac27$ at $y=0,1,2$.",
     "latex": "E[Y\\mid X=1]=0\\cdot\\frac27+1\\cdot\\frac37+2\\cdot\\frac27=1"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $3.5$\n\n**(b)** $1$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "cae95c9c-8ecd-4ad8-8797-8d59909cb6c1"
    }
   ],
   "id": "b2f029aa-c3ef-5062-ace7-5c64b91e4e43"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 5 · Does the mean change?",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "A1 table. Find $E[Y\\mid X=0]$ and compare with $E[Y\\mid X=1]=1$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Weights** $\\tfrac13,\\tfrac12,\\tfrac16$ (A1 Try it).",
     "latex": "E[Y\\mid X=0]=0+\\frac12+2\\cdot\\frac16=\\frac56"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "$\\tfrac56\\ne1$: the mean changes with $x$ → dependent.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac56$; dependent",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4dd905d4-d26c-570e-9caf-b60edc948251"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "C2 · $E[g(X)\\mid Y=y]$ and conditional variance",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "4bcfb3bb-db98-5dd2-8a1c-8a9fff83b343"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Same weights, but put $g(x)$ in front instead of $x$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "5ad2282c-1474-44fa-ad34-94fab76cd986"
    }
   ],
   "id": "a53bd412-4307-51f3-bb17-e20a842db996"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[g(X)\\mid Y=y]=\\sum_x g(x)\\,p_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "521d8228-b4de-531b-9305-7c7baa82412a"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid Y=y)=E[X^2\\mid Y=y]-\\big(E[X\\mid Y=y]\\big)^2",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "d7b622f9-e780-5131-986d-a3aacaf0b69a"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 6 · Conditional variance from a table",
   "prompt": "A1 table. Find $\\operatorname{Var}(Y\\mid X=1)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean** (C1).",
     "latex": "E[Y\\mid X=1]=1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Square** each value, same weights.",
     "latex": "E[Y^2\\mid X=1]=0\\cdot\\frac27+1\\cdot\\frac37+4\\cdot\\frac27=\\frac{11}7"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\operatorname{Var}(Y\\mid X=1)=\\frac{11}7-1^2=\\frac47"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac47$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "a25bde00-9c60-4121-8f33-54a29f5be927"
    }
   ],
   "id": "40cdda69-e37a-5154-8656-5b2f3fbd917d"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 6 · Dice, a function of $X$",
   "difficulty": "introductory",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$X$ = first die, $Y$ = sum. Find $E[X^2\\mid Y=7]$ and $E[2^X\\mid Y=7]$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Weights** $\\tfrac16$.",
     "latex": "E[X^2\\mid Y=7]=\\frac{1+4+9+16+25+36}{6}=\\frac{91}6"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Put $2^x$ in front.**",
     "latex": "E[2^X\\mid Y=7]=\\frac{2+4+8+16+32+64}{6}=\\frac{126}6=21"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac{91}6$; $21$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b7e2513f-be6a-57e2-8d2b-235a87cdceea"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "C3 · Total expectation (Lecture 23)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "255b3eeb-e1df-52bb-ae55-06e4d935c275"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "$E[X\\mid Y]$ (no \"$=y$\") is a **random variable**: write $g(y)=E[X\\mid Y=y]$, then $E[X\\mid Y]=g(Y)$. It is your best guess of $X$ once you see $Y$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "625ace99-ee24-45d3-afdd-300316ee5b2b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "bc2e9959-e3e6-4c56-8dd9-abb667d106c6"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c3e6207c-863f-5f73-acf7-a15abd307949"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
