  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 7 · Router modes ★ (Lecture 23)",
   "prompt": "A router is in normal mode or high-traffic mode, each with probability $\\tfrac12$. Packets per second $X$ are Poisson with mean $2$ in normal mode and $5$ in high mode. Find $E[X]$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Name the cases:** $Y=1$ normal, $Y=0$ high. A Poisson mean is its $\\lambda$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}E[X\\mid Y=1]=2,\\quad E[X\\mid Y=0]=5 \\\\ P(Y=1)=P(Y=0)=\\frac12\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Weight and add.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=2\\cdot\\frac12+5\\cdot\\frac12=3.5"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$3.5$",
   "citations": [
