   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "| | $x=1$ | $x=2$ | $x=3$ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $y=1$ | $0.10$ | $0.20$ | $0.10$ |\n| $y=2$ | $0.30$ | $0.10$ | $0.20$ |\n\n**(a)** Find $p_{X|Y}(x\\mid1)$, $E[X\\mid Y=1]$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid Y=1)$. (4 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $p_{X|Y}(x\\mid2)$ and $P(X\\ge2\\mid Y=2)$. (3 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $E[X\\mid Y=2]$. Are $X$ and $Y$ independent? (3 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Row $y=1$**, total $0.4$. **Divide.**",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid1)=\\frac14,\\ \\frac12,\\ \\frac14\\quad(x=1,2,3)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean, square, subtract.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}E[X\\mid Y=1]=\\frac14+1+\\frac34=2 \\\\ E[X^2\\mid Y=1]=\\frac14+2+\\frac94=4.5 \\\\ \\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid Y=1)=4.5-4=0.5\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Row $y=2$**, total $0.6$.",
     "latex": "p_{X|Y}(x\\mid2)=\\frac12,\\ \\frac16,\\ \\frac13"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Add** $x=2,3$.",
     "latex": "P(X\\ge2\\mid Y=2)=\\frac16+\\frac13=\\frac12"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=2]=\\frac12+\\frac26+\\frac36=\\frac{11}6"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "$2\\ne\\tfrac{11}6$: the mean changes with $y$ → **dependent**.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\tfrac14,\\tfrac12,\\tfrac14$; $2$; $0.5$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac12,\\tfrac16,\\tfrac13$; $\\tfrac12$\n\n**(c)** $\\tfrac{11}6$; dependent",
